Hello Typemill Team,

I would like to responsibly disclose 2 medium-severity authorization issue in Typemill as follow.

Issue 1:

Any authenticated user with mycontent:read (default roles: contributor, author, and above) can retrieve the full draft body of arbitrary pages, 
including pages they do not own and pages that are unpublished (HTTP 404 on the public frontend).

Write-side APIs for drafts/blocks enforce ownership when the role lacks global content:update. The draft read path only checks mycontent:
read and does not call the ownership check (userIsAllowed).

Issue 2:

Any authenticated user, including the lowest role “guest”, can retrieve metadata and navigation item objects for unpublished pages through API endpoints that only require public:read.
The same URLs return HTTP 404 in the public frontend. The API authorization path uses contentIsAllowed(), which only evaluates optional alloweduser/allowedrole fields and defaults to allow. 
It does not check whether the page is published / present in the live tree.

Attachments include detailed reports for both issues and a single Python PoC that confirms both findings against version 2.25.0.

Best regards.

