## Potential Risks & Compatibility

| Risk | Mitigation |
|---|---|
| Breaking legitimate external API clients that expect unpublished metadata | External API is documented for published content; unpublished access was unintended. The change aligns API behavior with the public frontend. |
| Contributors/authors can no longer read other users’ drafts through the public API | This is the intended behavior. Owners can still read their own drafts. Users with `content:read` can still read all drafts. |
| `getItemForUrl` returns 404 instead of 403 | Matches the public frontend and prevents information leakage. |
| Performance cost of loading metadata for every item in `getItemsForSlug` | Metadata is already loaded in other code paths; impact is minimal for typical result sets. |

---

## Summary

| # | Vulnerability | Confirmed | Severity | Fix Location |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Draft read path missing ownership check | Yes | Medium | `ControllerApiGlobals.php` (`getArticleContent`) |
| 2 | Public API endpoints expose unpublished content | Yes | Medium | `ControllerApiGlobals.php` + `Controller.php` (`publicApiIsAllowed` helper) |

**Recommended implementation order:**

1. Add `publicApiIsAllowed()` helper to `Controller.php`.
2. Apply the helper to the four public API endpoints in `ControllerApiGlobals.php`.
3. Add the ownership check to the `draft=true` branch of `getArticleContent()`.
4. Run the manual test matrix above.

No core files outside `/system/typemill/Controllers` are modified. No new dependencies are introduced.

