# Implementation Result

Date: 2026-09-18  
Status: **IMPLEMENTED AND VERIFIED**

## Files Changed

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `system/typemill/Controllers/Controller.php` | Added `publicApiIsAllowed()` helper |
| `system/typemill/Controllers/ControllerApiGlobals.php` | Applied helper to `getItemForUrl`, `getItemsForSlug`, `getArticleContent`, `getArticleMeta`; added ownership check to `draft=true` branch |

## Code Diff Summary

- `Controller.php` now exposes `publicApiIsAllowed($username, $userrole, $item, $pagemeta)` which returns `['allowed' => bool, 'reason' => string]`.
- The helper enforces: `content:read` users can see everything; unpublished pages are visible only to their owner with `mycontent:read`; published/modified pages still respect `alloweduser`/`allowedrole`.
- All four public API endpoints return **404** for unpublished disallowed items (matching the public frontend) and **403** for restricted published items.
- The `draft=true` branch in `getArticleContent()` now requires ownership when the caller lacks global `content:read`.

